    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d369">

                <pb facs="0456" n="1290" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1290"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 658.119/628</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Sweden</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Whitehouse</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-09-20T13:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 20, 1918, 1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 7.42 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2873. I have this morning presented to the Minister for Foreign Affairs a note
                    according to the instructions contained in your 1077, September 5, 3 p.m., and
                    1122, September 13, 8 p.m. Before doing so I consulted my colleagues who all
                    advised me to wait no longer as they feared there would be great delay before
                    all our different instructions could be brought into conformity.</p>
                <pb facs="0457" n="1291" xml:id="pg1291"/>
                <p>The Minister for Foreign Affairs said he would send me the statistics asked for
                    as soon as possible, but that he would be unable to comply with the request for
                    the text of any agreement with Germany. I do not think this last point need be
                    pressed as the Minister for Foreign Affairs gave me clearly to understand that
                    the coal agreement which expires September 30 was the only one still binding.
                    Stockholm to London.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Whitehouse</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
